<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 18 September, from 96 to 1970.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/domitian" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/domitian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">96 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,930 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Domitian is murdered and Nerva becomes emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domitian">Domitian</a> was stabbed to death in a palace conspiracy, and the Senate chose the elderly Nerva to succeed him. Nerva's adoption of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a> began the era of the 'Five Good Emperors'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">324 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,702 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantine defeats Licinius at Chrysopolis</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Constantine's victory over his co-emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licinius">Licinius</a> at Chrysopolis, across the Bosporus from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>, made him sole ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>. He soon refounded Byzantium as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1048">1048 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">978 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Byzantine-Georgian army fights the Seljuks at Kapetron</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Byzantine-Georgian army met a Seljuk raid into Byzantine-ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, led by Ibrahim Inal, half-brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughril">Tughril</a> I, at Kapetron. In the night battle Byzantine forces won on the flanks, but their Georgian allies were defeated in the centre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-seljuk-wars">Byzantine–Seljuk wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1180">1180 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">846 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Philip Augustus becomes king of France at fifteen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Philip II, the fifteen-year-old only son of King Louis VII, began his reign as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Later called Augustus for enlarging the crown lands, he won Normandy, Anjou, Maine and Poitou from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1204.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1454">1454 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">572 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Teutonic Knights defeat the Polish army at Chojnice</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near the town of Chojnice, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a> defeated a Polish army in the first year of the Thirteen Years' War. The war had begun when the Prussian estates rebelled against the Order and placed themselves under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casimir-iv-jagiellon">Casimir IV Jagiellon</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirteen-years-war-1454-1466">Thirteen Years' War (1454–1466)</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington lays the cornerstone of the US Capitol</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Washington laid the cornerstone of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitol</a> in a Masonic ceremony. Congress first met in the unfinished building in November 1800.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1850">1850 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">176 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President Fillmore signs the Fugitive Slave Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Part of the Compromise of 1850, the act required citizens of free states to help return people who had escaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, and denied them a jury trial. It turned many Northerners against slavery.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1970">1970 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jimi Hendrix dies in London aged 27</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Guitarist Jimi Hendrix died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> after taking barbiturates. In four years of fame he had transformed the electric guitar with his use of feedback, distortion and virtuoso technique.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 18 September <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/zhang-xianzhong"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zhang-xianzhong.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Zhang Xianzhong</span><span class="tp">1606–1647</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/samuel-johnson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/samuel-johnson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Samuel Johnson</span><span class="tp">1709–1784</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christian-viii-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christian-viii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christian VIII of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1786–1848</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/justinus-kerner"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/justinus-kerner.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Justinus Kerner</span><span class="tp">1786–1862</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-scullin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-scullin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James Scullin</span><span class="tp">1876–1953</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/seewoosagur-ramgoolam"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/seewoosagur-ramgoolam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Seewoosagur Ramgoolam</span><span class="tp">1900–1985</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 18 September <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-vii-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-vii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis VII of France</span><span class="tp">1120–1180</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-v-duke-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-v-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis V, Duke of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1315–1361</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/balsa-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/balsa-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Balša II</span><span class="tp">d. 1385</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leonhard-euler"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leonhard-euler.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leonhard Euler</span><span class="tp">1707–1783</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/voline"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/voline.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Voline</span><span class="tp">1882–1945</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dag-hammarskjold"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dag-hammarskjold.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dag Hammarskjöld</span><span class="tp">1905–1961</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
